Reset first_run in retro_unload_game so emulation restarts on relaunch.

retro_run() starts the emulator only `if (first_run)`, and first_run is
reset to true only by retro_init()/retro_deinit(). Frontends that keep the
core loaded across games and drive relaunch with retro_unload_game() +
retro_load_game() (no deinit/init) — e.g. REG-Station's in-process Libra
player — therefore leave first_run == false after the first game, so
emu.start() is never called on the second game: only the (frontend-drawn)
bezel appears, with no audio or video.

Reset first_run in retro_unload_game(). Harmless under RetroArch, which
closes the core the normal way and so already gets this from retro_deinit().

Anchored on the retro_unload_game() function header rather than on
`emu.unloadGame();` alone: that call appears in retro_reset() too, a few
lines above an equally plausible run of context, and an earlier version of
this patch applied cleanly there instead — leaving the real relaunch path
untouched and the bug fully intact (verified on hardware: every flycast game
after the first showed bezel only, no audio, no video, while the core's own
log was byte-identical to the working first launch).

--- a/shell/libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/shell/libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -2437,6 +2437,12 @@
 void retro_unload_game()
 {
 	INFO_LOG(COMMON, "Flycast unloading game");
+
+	// REG-Linux: reset first_run so the next retro_run() calls emu.start()
+	// again. Libra keeps the core loaded across games (no retro_deinit/init),
+	// and emu.start() is gated on first_run — only retro_init/deinit reset it.
+	first_run = true;
+
 	emu.unloadGame();
 	dreampotato::term();
 	game_data.clear();
